==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|prædatory||archaic}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|praedātōrius}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɹedətəɹi/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-predatory.oga|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, or relating to a [[predator]].
#* {{quote-web|en|date=July 3 2021|author=Phil McNulty|work=BBC Sport|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/51198691|title=Ukraine 0-4 England|passage={{w|Harry Kane}} was back to his '''predatory''' best after struggling in the group stage, following up his goal against Germany by poking home a superb pass from {{w|Raheem Sterling}} after only four minutes.}}
# Living by [[preying]] on other [[living]] [[animal]]s.
#: {{syn|en|predaceous|predacious}}
#* {{RQ:Burroughs Son of Tarzan|chapter=IX|passage=The mark of his father’s early life was strong upon him and enhanced by months of association with beasts, from whom the imitative faculty of youth had absorbed a countless number of little mannerisms of the '''predatory''' creatures of the wild.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} [[exploiting|Exploiting]] or [[victimizing]] others for [[personal]] [[gain]].
#: {{co|en|{{w|predatory lending|'''predatory''' lending}}}}
#: {{co|en|'''predatory''' inclusion}}
#: {{co|en|{{w|predatory publishing|'''predatory''' publishing}}}}
#* {{RQ:Booth Darkest|chapter=7|passage=One very important section of the denizens of Darkest England are the criminals and the semi-criminals. They are more or less '''predatory''', and are at present shepherded by the police and punished by the gaoler.}}
#* {{RQ:Sinclair Jungle|chapter=31|passage=The purpose of government was the guarding of property-rights, the perpetuation of ancient force and modern fraud. Or was it marriage? Marriage and prostitution were two sides of one shield, the '''predatory''' man’s exploitation of the sex-pleasure.}}

